---
// Technical leadership responsibilities.
---
<section class="section wrap" id="leadership">
  <div class="sec-head"><p class="kicker">Leadership</p><h2>Leading teams, not just code</h2></div>
  <div class="lead-grid">
    <aside class="lead-card">
      <span class="arch-ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="3"/><circle cx="5" cy="17" r="2.5"/><circle cx="19" cy="17" r="2.5"/><path d="M10.3 9.6 6.4 15M13.7 9.6l3.9 5.4M7.5 17h9"/></svg></span>
      <h3>Technical Leadership</h3>
      <p class="lead-label">Coordinating across</p>
      <ul class="lead-teams"><li>Clients</li><li>Development</li><li>QA</li><li>DevOps</li><li>Infrastructure</li><li>Security</li></ul>
    </aside>
    <ol class="lead-list">
      <li><span><strong>Lead</strong> teams of developers across design, development and delivery.</span></li>
      <li><span><strong>Mentor</strong> developers on Java, Spring Boot, architecture and engineering practices.</span></li>
      <li><span><strong>Act as technical SPOC</strong> between clients and engineering teams.</span></li>
      <li><span><strong>Coordinate</strong> Development, QA, DevOps, Infrastructure and Security.</span></li>
      <li><span><strong>Drive</strong> technical decisions and resolve complex production issues.</span></li>
      <li><span><strong>Establish</strong> engineering standards and review practices.</span></li>
      <li><span><strong>Enable</strong> teams to adopt AI-assisted development responsibly.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
